# Did the first registration after the last relocalize / initialpose guess
# succeed? Served by localizer_node (the workspace's syncai_localizer) on the
# relative name `relocalize_check`, in the bare robot_id namespace, so it lands
# on <robot_id>/relocalize_check (not <robot_id>/localizer/relocalize_check).
# The backend polls it after a Relocalize call, because that call's success is
# only a receipt. Moved here from SyncAI-Fast-LIO2's `interface` package in
# 2026-09 with Relocalize.
#
# code 0 asks the real question. code 1 always answers valid: true, for
# callers that only want to know the service is up. Any other code is
# treated as 0.
#
# This is the ONLY quality signal the stack has. RobotState.localization_valid
# is TF-presence only and reads true against a map the robot was never
# localized in; do not "fix" it from anything but this.
int32 code
---
bool valid
